{"duration_api_ms":154644,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9ea2f805-13fd-45b8-a465-81904b3d1988","total_cost_usd":0.127937,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19211},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":20849,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":20849,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11841,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.127937,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":19211,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic wallets. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into an ASCII seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP falls under the GPL License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet satoshis. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone. This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the Mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits. With more entropy, security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT/32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words:\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"for the generation of deterministic wallets\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected undefined term to match BIP39's purpose\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed character encoding issue and formalized contraction\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo and standardized section heading capitalization\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo and corrected entropy specification per BIP39\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected invalid range and unit per BIP39 standard\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT/32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected nonexistent hash algorithm to BIP39 standard\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This checksum is appended to the initial entropy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Clarified confusing language; appended adds to end not start\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected bit group size per 0-2047 encoding range requirement\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"in a multiple of 23 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 requires entropy multiples of 32 for checksum calculation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"1024-2048 byts\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 standard specifies 128-256 bits not 1024-2048 bytes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT/32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"its SHA652 hash\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 uses SHA256; SHA652 is not a valid hash algorithm\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"for the generation of deterministic wallets\",\n      \"corrects\": \"for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 generates mnemonics for wallet generation not UTOXs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047\",\n      \"corrects\": \"groups of 12 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"11-bit groups encode 0-2047 range; 12-bit groups encode 0-4095\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":152296,"type":"result","duration_ms":159208,"uuid":"e4957e89-c819-44a2-8cf3-4630df69da1e","ttft_stream_ms":5254,"time_to_request_ms":4561,"first_content_frame_ms":5254,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
